# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# Local dev:  a SQLite file. Nothing to install, nothing to sign up for.
# Production: a libSQL/Turso URL (same SQL dialect, works on serverless).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL="file:./data/pedr.db"
# DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=""            # only needed for a remote libsql:// URL

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no session secret. A session token is 32 random bytes and only its
# SHA-256 reaches the database, so there is nothing to sign and nothing here to
# rotate or leak.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Without it the parser still works — it just runs the deterministic
# pass only. With it, messy dumps get a second, much smarter pass.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# Where this instance is reachable. Used in the calendar feed and reminders,
# and for every canonical URL, sitemap entry and share card. On Vercel this
# falls back to VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL if you leave it unset.
APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Optional: protects /api/cron/* so only your scheduler can call it.
# CRON_SECRET=""

# Optional: the cron digest is POSTed here. Without it the run still reports
# what it found, it just does not send anything.
# REMINDER_WEBHOOK_URL=""
